.TH SWAPDEVNAME 3 "June 3, 2026"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
swapdevname \- kernel swapdev to device pathname
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdlib.h>
.sp
\fBint retval = swapdevname\fP(\fIchar *buf, int len\fP)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B swapdevname
function returns the kernel variable \fIswapdev\fP as a pathname (e.g. /dev/xp0b)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
If sysctl(3) fails (kernel lacks VM_SWAPDEV) OR
if the DBM database (/var/run/dev) can not be opened OR if 
\fIswapdev\fP can not be found in the database 
.B swapdevname
will use the traditional value \fB/dev/swap\fP
.sp
.B devname
prints a warning message to stderr if the device database can not be opened.
.PP
.SH BUGS
If 
.B len
is not large enough only \fIlen - 1\fP bytes will be placed in \fIbuf\fP 
followed by a terminating '\\0'
.SH RETURN VALUE
.sp
.nf
 retval < 0 retval bytes unused in \fIbuf\fP
 retval = 0 the string + '\\0' exactly fit in \fIbuf\fP
 retval > 0 \fIbuf\fP is retval bytes too small
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
snprintf(3), sysctl(3), devname(3), dev_mkdb(8), sysctl(8)
.SH HISTORY
The
.B swapdevname
function appeared in \fB2.11BSD 35th Anniversary Edition\fP.
